  class Point
  {
  public:
    void setX(double x);
  };
};

int main()
{
  ros::NodeHandle nh;
  nh.set_name("geometry_msgs/Point");
  nh.set_namespace("geometry_msgs");
}
int main()
{
  ros::NodeHandle nh;
  nh.set_name("geometry_msgs/Point");
  nh.set_namespace("geometry_msgs");
}
```

In this example, the `nh` object is an instance of the `NodeHandle` class, which is defined in the `geometry_msgs` namespace. The `set_name` function is used to set the name of the node to "geometry_msgs/Point", and the `set_namespace` function is used to set the namespace to "geometry_msgs". This is a common pattern in ROS for defining nodes and topics within a specific namespace.

The `geometry_msgs` namespace is a standard namespace used for messages related to geometry and poses in ROS. It is not a unique or custom namespace and is widely recognized by other nodes and libraries that interact with geometry-related data.

